WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 0.1 · Start Here: Your Founder Journey
How this course works

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Decide in the order founders need to: each course builds on the one before.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
This course is a path through the decisions a founder makes, in the order they are usually needed. Each step builds on the one before, so you lay foundations instead of repairing them later.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four courses, one order

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:41.204
Clarify: Why should this exist, and what change will you pursue? Modules 00 to 02. For example: A repair café writes its purpose and the change it wants before choosing a legal form.

6
00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:54.385
Organise: Who will decide, who will do the work and how it will run day to day. Modules 03 to 05. For example: Two co-founders agree who approves spending and how volunteers are welcomed.

7
00:00:54.385 --> 00:01:07.196
Prove & Show: How you will know it works, and how you will show it. Modules 06 to 08. For example: A tutoring service picks three signs of progress, a name and a simple logo.

8
00:01:07.196 --> 00:01:20.467
Protect: How you will stay solvent, legal and safe from the start. Modules 09 and 10. For example: A youth club drafts a first-year budget and a safeguarding policy before opening.

9
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:21.467
Why the order matters

10
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:27.881
1. Most early questions depend on what you are for and who you serve.

11
00:01:27.881 --> 00:01:33.556
2. Deciding in order saves rebuilding your registration, budget or brand later.

12
00:01:33.556 --> 00:01:40.230
3. You can see what to do now and what can wait.

13
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:41.230
How each lesson works

14
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:46.163
1. A short video, a written explanation and an exercise.

15
00:01:46.163 --> 00:01:51.467
2. Your answers save into your founding pack as you go.

16
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:58.881
3. Download each module as a PDF to share with a co-founder or adviser.

17
00:01:59.281 --> 00:01:59.881
What to avoid

18
00:01:59.881 --> 00:02:05.556
Jumping to registration or money before knowing what you are for.

19
00:02:05.556 --> 00:02:09.748
Trying to finish everything in one sitting.

20
00:02:09.748 --> 00:02:17.163
Treating a first draft as final: mark what is uncertain and come back.

21
00:02:17.763 --> 00:02:19.563
You write your priority module, what it depends on and when you will reach it.

22
00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:23.563
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:25.063 --> 00:02:28.163
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
